Z||000000||BAM-BAM||04-17-2000||10:08 PM||||   I am about to replace the upper and lower ball joints on my 85GT. In the book it says to examine the lower control arm for excessive ware. What exactly, constitutes excessive? Then, if it is excessive, replace the entire control arm. Where can I get a new lower control arm? I just want it to be done right the first time. TIA for any help or advice.<P> Thanx, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||04-17-2000||10:46 PM||||Excessive wear would be damage to the control arm or worn bushings.. If damaged you need to get a used one from someone or a junk yard. If bushings are bad just replace them. I changed all my bushings to polyurethane. If you are replacing the ball joints, make sure you get the MOOG for the top. They are slotted to allow camber adjustments. The bottom ball joints if original are spot welded in 2 places. These need to be ground off so you can remove the ball joint. The new ones have to be pressed in. Since you most likely will have to remove the lower control arm to change the ball joint I would suggest new bushings. Rubber retains stock feel, poly will stiffen up the front and have less understeer. I have actually just finished replacing my entire suspension with new ball joints,bushings, tie rods, springs and shocks, larger sway bar, and bearings/rotors.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 04-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||04-17-2000||11:29 PM||||  Thanks for the advise. That is exactly what I am working on. I am putting together all the necessary components to rebuild the entire front end. I already have the replacement Poly bushings for the control arms and swaybar. Next wiil be KYB gas shocks<BR>and Eibach lowering springs 1" drop. Baretta brake upgrade. Once I have it all then the fun begins. Not to mention I will be replacing the upper and lower ball joints.<P> Thanx, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||12
